#! clause: LA
#! mode: static
#! stage: parse
# Grammar-parity (§6.4): a nested `if` (with its own `end`) as the first statement of a
# final `else` body is valid when `else` is followed by a separator — distinct from `else if`
# (an elif). The Lezer grammar must accept it too (probed against the engine).
if a then
  x = 1
else
  if b then
    x = 2
  end
end
